{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTAjmxcnzEAGtqsJ3bSK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M2UVXEq5xffhfJEMjvLUHh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; find / -name figure_manifest.schema.json 2>/dev/null | head; sed -n 50,60p paper.tex; cat figures/overview_pipeline.prompts.json | head -20; cat scripts/build_figures.py | head -60; cat figures/main_comparison.pdf.prov.json; ls .claude/skills/validate-paper"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7502,"cache_read_input_tokens":42989,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7502,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afcdc791-b4aa-4206-89ff-ecce3395fcc8","uuid":"cdee5a73-0b48-49ad-bb17-373ace1ced69","timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:53:04.161Z","request_id":"req_011CgTAjmPdb6R4hSFL2Hw4K"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M2UVXEq5xffhfJEMjvLUHh","type":"tool_result","content":"/workspace/paper/.claude/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\begin{figure}[t]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth]{figures/overview_pipeline.png}\n\\caption{Overview of the study. A connected graph ($6\\le n\\le 30$) is reduced to five relabeling-invariant statistics; a ridge model predicts log cover time, which is compared with a Monte Carlo label. The $2m(n-1)$ bound, a constant predictor and a shuffled-target control are scored through the same pipeline: per-graph clipped log error $\\rightarrow$ family mean $\\rightarrow$ family-macro mean $\\rightarrow$ mean over seeded episodes.}\n\\label{fig:overview}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\section{Related Work}\n\\paragraph{Worst-case bounds.} The $2m(n-1)$ bound of Aleliunas et al.\\ \\citep{Aleliunas1979RandomWU} follows by summing commute times, each at most $2m$, over the $n-1$ edges of a spanning tree. Feige's upper bound, $(4/27+o(1))n^3$, is attained by lollipop-like graphs, and his companion lower bound, $(1+o(1))\\,n\\ln n$, is attained by the complete graph \\citep{Feige1995ATU,Feige1995ATL}. Together these delimit the possible range of cover times for a given $n$ but are worst-case over all connected graphs; they are not intended as point predictions for a given graph. Lov\\'asz's survey on random walks on graphs \\citep{Lovasz2001RandomWO} collects the hitting-time and commute-time machinery behind such bounds, and the electrical-network view of random walks \\citep{Doyle1984RandomWA} relates commute times to effective resistances. Our comparison against $2m(n-1)$ therefore measures how much a worst-case guarantee costs as a predictor on small graphs; it is not a criticism of the bound, which remains valid.\n{\n  \"attempted_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n  \"reason\": \"generate-concept-figure exited non-zero (rc=1)\",\n  \"run_log_path\": \"concept_figure_run.log\",\n  \"status\": \"failed\"\n}\n\"\"\"Build the main comparison figure (and the concept-figure placeholder) from paper_data.json.\"\"\"\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nFIG = ROOT / \"figures\"\nFIG.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n\n# @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics]]\nmetrics = json.loads((ROOT / \"paper_data.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))[\"final_evaluation\"][\"metrics\"]\n\nrows = [  # label, metric key, color\n    (\"Five-stat.\\nridge\", \"macro_log_mae\", \"#1f5fa8\"),\n    (\"Constant\\n(train\\ngeo-mean)\", \"const_macro_log_mae\", \"#c9a227\"),\n    (\"Ridge vs.\\nshuffled\\ntargets\", \"shuffle_macro_log_mae\", \"#b5533c\"),\n    (\"Bound\\n$2m(n-1)$\", \"bound_macro_log_mae\", \"#6b6b6b\"),\n]\n\n\ndef main_comparison():\n    plt.rcParams.update({\"font.size\": 11, \"axes.labelsize\": 11, \"xtick.labelsize\": 10, \"ytick.labelsize\": 10})\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.0, 3.4))\n    xs = range(len(rows))\n    vals = [metrics[k] for _, k, _ in rows]\n    bars = ax.bar(xs, vals, color=[c for _, _, c in rows], width=0.62)\n    for b, v in zip(bars, vals):\n        ax.text(b.get_x() + b.get_width() / 2, v + 0.03, f\"{v:.3f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=10)\n    ax.set_xticks(list(xs))\n    ax.set_xticklabels([r[0] for r in rows])\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"Family-macro log MAE\", fontsize=11)\n    ax.set_ylim(0, max(vals) * 1.14)\n    ax.spines[[\"top\", \"right\"]].set_visible(False)\n    ax.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.25)\n    ax.set_axisbelow(True)\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(FIG / \"main_comparison.pdf\")\n    fig.savefig(FIG / \"main_comparison.png\", dpi=300)\n    plt.close(fig)\n\n\ndef concept_placeholder():\n    # Never clobber the orchestrator-rendered concept figure.\n    if (ROOT / \".concept_figure_complete\").exists():\n        return\n    png = FIG / \"overview_pipeline.png\"\n    log = FIG / \"overview_pipeline.prompts.json\"\n    if log.exists() and log.read_text().strip() not in (\"\", \"{}\"):\n        return\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(11, 3.2))\n    ax.text(0.5, 0.5, \"overview_pipeline (placeholder)\", ha=\"center\", va=\"center\")\n    ax.axis(\"off\")\n    fig.savefig(png, dpi=220)\n    plt.close(fig)\n    log.write_text(\"{}\\n\")\n\n\n{\n  \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\",\n  \"artifact\": {\"path\": \"figures/main_comparison.pdf\", \"kind\": \"figure\"},\n  \"derived_from\": [\n    \"@evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics]]\",\n    \"@evidence[[scripts/build_figures.py]]\"\n  ]\n}\nSKILL.md\nscripts\ntemplates","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afcdc791-b4aa-4206-89ff-ecce3395fcc8","uuid":"49bb56e4-d64e-4e42-bf9b-fc96b824d54d","timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:53:04.421Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/workspace/paper/.claude/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\begin{figure}[t]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth]{figures/overview_pipeline.png}\n\\caption{Overview of the study. A connected graph ($6\\le n\\le 30$) is reduced to five relabeling-invariant statistics; a ridge model predicts log cover time, which is compared with a Monte Carlo label. The $2m(n-1)$ bound, a constant predictor and a shuffled-target control are scored through the same pipeline: per-graph clipped log error $\\rightarrow$ family mean $\\rightarrow$ family-macro mean $\\rightarrow$ mean over seeded episodes.}\n\\label{fig:overview}\n\\end{figure}\n\n\\section{Related Work}\n\\paragraph{Worst-case bounds.} The $2m(n-1)$ bound of Aleliunas et al.\\ \\citep{Aleliunas1979RandomWU} follows by summing commute times, each at most $2m$, over the $n-1$ edges of a spanning tree. Feige's upper bound, $(4/27+o(1))n^3$, is attained by lollipop-like graphs, and his companion lower bound