{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ybsA9Mz8e1ZVYbzg5nyvM","type":"tool_result","content":"116:Test graphs are content-hash disjoint from the graphs visible during model selection. Labels are Monte Carlo estimates of $C(G)$ computed by the evaluator from simple-random-walk simulations started equally often from every vertex, with about $300$ walks per graph in total; each label comes with a standard error. % @evidence[[protocol_facts.json#MC_WALKS]]\n285:Aggregation is fixed before evaluation with equal weights: per-graph error $\\min(|\\ln(\\hat y/y)|,10)$, mean within family, unweighted mean over families, mean over episodes. A failed episode would contribute $10$ to the macro error and a perturbation deviation of $10^{6}$; none is recorded here. Monte Carlo labels simulate walks from every start vertex equally often, about $300$ walks per graph in total (run-time \\texttt{MC\\_WALKS}$=300$), with the standard error computed from the sample standard deviation of observed cover times. % @evidence[[protocol_facts.json#MC_WALKS]] @evidence[[protocol_facts.json#ERR_CLIP]]\n315:\\subsection{LLM Usage}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afcdc791-b4aa-4206-89ff-ecce3395fcc8","uuid":"d5d8facf-72a8-48a9-b131-c786c6515c91","timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:53:48.927Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"116:Test graphs are content-hash disjoint from the graphs visible during model selection. Labels are Monte Carlo estimates of $C(G)$ computed by the evaluator from simple-random-walk simulations started equally often from every vertex, with about $300$ walks per graph in total; each label comes with a standard error. % @evidence[[protocol_facts.json#MC_WALKS]]\n285:Aggregation is fixed before evaluation with equal weights: per-graph error $\\min(|\\ln(\\hat y/y)|,10)$, mean within family, unweighted mean over families, mean over episodes. A failed episode would contribute $10$ to the macro error and a perturbation deviation