- **Label-noise claim:** the Discussion no longer says the noise floor is non-negligible for the slowest families. It now says per-graph standard errors were not retained, so noise on those graphs cannot be assessed. I also corrected one Introduction sentence that called the gap "small relative to Monte Carlo label noise". It now reads "large relative to the median Monte Carlo label noise", matching the 0.029 median.

